{"kind":"assert","text":"Design note for e5b86654, draft 1, is written. Branch\n`planner/client-primitive-note-20261113`, commit 68a4ae3b, file\n`notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md`, in the planner worktree\n`planner-client-primitive-20261113`. The hold on main (b6f9f350)\nkeeps it off main until the cutover lands. Hugh ratifies it.\n\nThe note rules each of the twelve items. Section 15 maps them.\nFive rulings carry the design:\n\n1. The client signs only when the member submits. No timer signs.\n   A request with no answer returns to its slot when its signing\n   dies, 6 minutes at the default lifetime.\n2. `mismatch` and `Settlement` keep their shapes. The replica\n   reads which intent holds a key. A client with no replica\n   settles each kept envelope, at most 8 reads. No K item.\n3. `refused` stays terminal for capacity and loses its finality.\n   A `refused` record moves to `accepted` on a receipt or on a\n   folded entry. `settle` asks the scope while a copy is in\n   flight. A member cannot fill a shared store with refusals.\n4. A custody record takes version 2 and holds the signings of\n   one request. `send` takes `resign: true`. A caller that does\n   not pass it gets today's behavior, so MCP does not change.\n5. Order: C1 (custody version 2), then NF-5, then C2 replica,\n   C3 requests, C4 slots and drafts. NF-5 stays held until Hugh\n   ratifies the note, and then waits only for C1.\n\nThe status of a request is a function of the replica, the\ncustody record and the clock. It has five values: `recorded`,\n`other-recorded`, `pending`, `withdrawn` and `refused`.\n\nNo build is placed. I file one request per step after Hugh\nratifies.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}